{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I had ox and donkey.</b> My father said to me: 'of the dew of heaven and of the fat places of the earth.' This — it is neither from heaven nor from earth." "<b>Ox and donkey.</b> It is the way of the world to say of many cattle 'ox' — a person says to his fellow 'the rooster crowed at night,' and does not say 'the roosters crowed.'" "<b>That I may send to tell my lord.</b> To inform that I am coming to you." "<b>That I may find favor in your eyes.</b> For I am whole with you and seek your love."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:40.447200740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}